# Vendored/runtime-managed plugin trees — installed by the tools themselves
# on first run (zsh-autosuggestions only tracks the single script file).
# NOTE: .config/tmux/plugins/** is intentionally NOT listed here — those
# paths are fetched via .chezmoiexternal.toml (git-repo externals for tpm
# and catppuccin) and must remain chezmoi-managed for that to apply.
.config/1Password/**
.ssh/1Password/**
.config/tmux/plugins/**

# Defense in depth: never let chezmoi apply raw SSH private/public key
# material into ~/.ssh on any device, even if one somehow lands in the
# source tree despite the .gitignore guard. authorized_keys and
# allowed_signers are plain pubkey listings, not standalone key files, and
# are intentionally excluded from this rule.
.ssh/*.priv
.ssh/*.pem
.ssh/*.pub
.ssh/id_rsa*
.ssh/id_ed25519*
.ssh/id_ecdsa*
.ssh/id_dsa*

# Machine-local mutable state — deliberately NOT managed. known_hosts is
# rewritten by ssh itself on every first connection to a new host, so
# managing it guarantees permanent drift: every `chezmoi apply` would revert
# host keys this machine legitimately learned, and every new host would show
# up as a spurious diff. known_hosts.old is ssh-keygen -R's backup file.
.ssh/known_hosts
.ssh/known_hosts.old

# Repo-only docs — not meant to be applied to $HOME
README.md
